<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (There is a place each of us is looking for. Not lost, exactly - more like imagined. A sense of space, of belonging, that we recognise without being able to name. A somewhere we have never quite reached.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
100 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (For Mansi Gupta, that search begins in Delhi.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
101 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (Born and raised in the city, her understanding of place has always been inseparable from its trees. The banyan she played beneath at school. The amaltas in bloom outside her grandmother's house. The jamuns lining the paths at India Gate. They became more than landmarks; they became the way she remembered the city itself.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
102 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (Over time, walking replaced destination. She wandered through the orderly avenues of Lutyens' Delhi, )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
103 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (the crowded lanes of Nai Sarak, the forgotten corners of Connaught Place, and the forests that continue to exist within the city. Years of moving slowly through familiar places changed the way she looked. What remained were not complete landscapes, but fragments: the curve of a trunk, the rhythm of branches, a horizon, a colour, the memory of light.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
104 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
105 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (Across the series Be Here Now, Light in Shade and Nowhere, Elsewhere, her work explores different ways of inhabiting a landscape: through attention, through memory, and through the enduring search for places that continue to shape us long after we have left them.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
